<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shimla</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Simla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shimla, formerly Simla, is a city in the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It grew after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-nepalese-war">Anglo-Nepalese War</a> of 1814–1816 on land taken from the hill states, and from 1864 it was the summer capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>. The Simla Conference of 1914 and the Simla Agreement of 1972 were held there. It gave its name to the surrounding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simla-hill-states">Simla Hill States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shimla.jpg" alt="Shimla" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Navneet Sharma · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landscape_of_Shimla_,_Himachal_Pradesh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
